WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.518 --> 00:00:03.544
One named folder per ONT library: Each ONCO-style library has fastq_pass and pod5_pass. This demo restores three libraries from their saved ONT project.

2
00:00:03.544 --> 00:00:11.227
Matching POD5 is selected: Each library keeps its own passed signal reads. Compatible Dorado and classifier models are required; these are synthetic fixtures.

3
00:00:11.227 --> 00:00:19.070
1 · Drag samples: Synthetic example: ONCO-001 → MARLIN; ONCO-002 → Sturgeon. For real data use clinical records; never infer diagnosis from names.

4
00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:27.020
Unknown is separate from Cancer or Normal: Cancer/Normal records the clinical role. These columns only choose a CpG classifier. Return unsuitable samples to Unknown / do not classify.

5
00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:35.453
2 · Save the chosen group: Choose MARLIN and save. Its new project contains only ONCO-001.

6
00:00:35.453 --> 00:00:39.106
2 · Save the chosen group: Choose Sturgeon and save ONCO-002 separately. The other group and Unknown sample are excluded.

7
00:00:39.106 --> 00:00:47.812
Confirm your Sturgeon license: Only acknowledge this after obtaining Sturgeon and accepting its terms. This demonstration uses synthetic resources.

8
00:00:47.812 --> 00:00:52.718
3 · Run only when ready: Use valid POD5 and compatible models, resolve checks and license requirements, then click Run explicitly. This demo stops after saving.
